;; records.corpus -- REMAINING record/deftype/reify gaps after the S3
;; type system landed (the conforming bulk was promoted to
;; corpus/records.corpus). Self-contained forms.
;;
;; EMPTY as of W3d2: every form this area ever carried now conforms and
;; has been promoted. Record metadata went first -- S5/M3 made records
;; IObj (see src/builtins/meta.rs's `is_iobj`) and that row moved to
;; corpus/metadata.corpus; S6 promoted `clojure.lang.IRecord` as a class
;; token the same way; D1 built `reify` and promoted three more
;; (`.toString`, protocol-fn dispatch, `record?`); W3d2 gave the anonymous
;; type the protocol keys it names (src/types.rs's `TypeDef::protocols`)
;; and promoted the last one, `satisfies?` of a `reify`d protocol, to
;; corpus/records.corpus's tail as well.
;;
;; The file is kept rather than deleted so the next record/deftype/reify
;; divergence has an obvious home -- an area with zero forms is a healthy
;; ledger entry, not a missing one.
